{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-19848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\frac{1!\\,2!}{3!\\,4!\\,5!}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/state.json" "file_sha256" "845b2d73aa3662818d425ad2d56c959f0ebc21f6c2644ecbef49300a09b49f6a"} {"question" "q-19848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that $5!=5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2!.$ Then, we can cancel the $2!$ that occur in both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1!\\,2!}{3!\\,4!\\,5!} & =\\frac{1\\cdot 2!}{(3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1)(4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1)(5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2!)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot \\cancel{2!}}{3\\cdot 2\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot \\cancel{2!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8\\,640}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/state.json" "file_sha256" "845b2d73aa3662818d425ad2d56c959f0ebc21f6c2644ecbef49300a09b49f6a"} {"question" "q-19848" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "699c8e53ddc223ab89e100f953ec4f27274b0bac562d94e11f00d3e69d6cfabe"} {"question" "q-19848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/state.json" "file_sha256" "845b2d73aa3662818d425ad2d56c959f0ebc21f6c2644ecbef49300a09b49f6a"} {"question" "q-19848" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{3\\,250}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4\\,320}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{520}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{60}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{8\\,640}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" 