idget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/state.json" "file_sha256" "845b2d73aa3662818d425ad2d56c959f0ebc21f6c2644ecbef49300a09b49f6a"} {"question" "q-122043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{5}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{5}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/state.json" "file_sha256" "845b2d73aa3662818d425ad2d56c959f0ebc21f6c2644ecbef49300a09b49f6a"} {"question" "q-122043" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/state.json" "file_sha256" "845b2d73aa3662818d425ad2d56c959f0ebc21f6c2644ecbef49300a09b49f6a"} {"question" "q-124393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$5!\\,0!=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/state.json" "file_sha256" "845b2d73aa3662818d425ad2d56c959f0ebc21f6c2644ecbef49300a09b49f6a"} {"question" "q-124393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given expression is a product of two factorials.\n\n- Computing $5!$ using the definition, we get\n\n$$\n5!=5\\cdot 4\\cdot 3\\cdot 2\\cdot 1=120.\n$$\n\n- By definition, the factorial of zero equals one:\n\n$$\n0!=1\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the given expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5!\\,0! & =120\\cdot 1=120\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977501/state.json" "file_sha256" "845b2d73aa3662818d425ad2d56c959f0ebc21f6c2644ecbef49300a09b49f6a"} {"question" "q-124393" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" 